C. MODALS: ALWAYS ABOVE PAGE CONTENT
Find the shared modal/dialog implementation used by Add Evidence File, Add Timeline Step, and any other action that opens the same type of overlay. Search for dialog/overlay usages rather than relying on names.
- Fix the root cause, not one z-index value. Render overlays through a portal to document.body with position: fixed; inset: 0 where the architecture supports it, so transformed, filtered, sticky, or overflow-hidden ancestors cannot clip them or stack above them. If a portal is not feasible, explain why and confirm that no ancestor causes clipping or a stacking/containing-context problem.
- Define one documented z-index scale in shared CSS variables or constants and reuse it in the touched files: page content < sticky header < header dropdowns/notification popovers < modal backdrop < modal dialog < popovers/select menus opened inside the modal < toast. Add no arbitrary competing z-index values.
- Center the dialog against the viewport. Width: the existing max width, limited by calc(100vw - 2rem). Height: max-height calc(100vh - 2rem), then calc(100dvh - 2rem) where supported. Use overflow-y: auto and overscroll-behavior: contain.
